  ($f0_0$blog_office_costs_20261019$f0_0$, $f0_1$office-rental-costs-midrand$f0_1$, $f0_2$Office Rental Costs in Midrand: Build Your Occupancy Budget$f0_2$, $f0_3$Budget for office occupation using dated unit examples, clear base-rent calculations and a checklist of recurring and initial costs.$f0_3$, $f0_4$<p>Build an office budget from the space your team needs, the agreed area and rate, and the charges and work required to occupy it. An advertised rental per square metre is a starting figure, not a complete monthly bill.</p>
<p>This guide supports our <a href="/offices">offices to rent in Midrand guide</a>. Use it to prepare a budget before asking for a written, unit-specific quote.</p>
<h2>Start with a dated base-rent calculation</h2>
<p>For an area-based rental, multiply the agreed rentable area by the agreed monthly rate per square metre. Keep the measurement basis and VAT treatment attached to that calculation.</p>
<p>For example, the <a href="/vacancies/cms4oiw4v0004n60127izdqzj">Sunbird ground-floor office listing</a>, checked on 19 October 2026, publishes 500.66 m&sup2; at R120 per m&sup2; per month. Multiplication gives an indicative base rental of R60,079.20 per month. It does not establish an all-inclusive quote, confirm VAT treatment or guarantee that the unit is still available.</p>
<p>A second published example is <a href="/vacancies/cms4oiw500005n6011rnzc2hb">Unit 1, 1 Weaver Avenue</a>: 266 m&sup2; at R105 per m&sup2; per month, giving R27,930 in indicative monthly base rent. These are different spaces, not evidence of a market average or a like-for-like price comparison.</p>
<h2>Separate recurring charges from move-in costs</h2>
<p>Ask the leasing team to identify each applicable item as included, separately charged, metered, once-off or not applicable. A blank line is an unanswered question, not a zero cost.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Recurring occupancy:</strong> base rent, applicable recoveries, utilities, parking, connectivity and any separately charged services.</li>
<li><strong>Initial cash requirements:</strong> deposit or other agreed security, any advance amounts, relocation, fit-out, furniture and connection costs.</li>
<li><strong>Future commitments:</strong> agreed escalation dates, maintenance responsibilities, changes in service use and any end-of-occupation work described in the proposed lease.</li>
</ul>
<p>Do not assume a deposit amount, escalation percentage or landlord contribution. Obtain those figures for the selected unit and proposed term. Read the written terms with your own advisers where needed.</p>
<h2>Budget for the workplace you will actually use</h2>
<p>The right office area depends on your layout, staff attendance, private rooms, meeting needs, storage and circulation. A larger floor plate is not automatically more economical because its advertised rate is lower. Use a current floor plan to test how much of the space serves your brief.</p>
<p>Check what is already fitted and what must change. Furniture, reception, meeting rooms, cabling and equipment may create different costs in two offices with similar advertised areas. The <a href="/blog/office-floor-plan-fit-out-checklist-midrand">floor-plan and fit-out checklist</a> helps turn those questions into a scope of work.</p>
<h2>Compare a conventional office with a serviced option</h2>
<p>If you are considering OnPoint, compare a written package against the conventional-office budget using the same team size and service requirements. Advertised meeting rooms, furniture options or tenant credits do not establish unlimited or included use. See our <a href="/blog/serviced-vs-conventional-offices-midrand">serviced versus conventional office comparison</a>.</p>
<h2>Keep the quote and the live schedule together</h2>
<p>Use the <a href="/offices#compare-spaces">live office comparison</a> and <a href="/vacancies?sector=Office">current office vacancies</a> for the latest published entries. An advertised date or “Immediately” remains subject to leasing confirmation. Listing photographs can show proposed works and do not replace a viewing.</p>
<p>If your requirement also includes warehousing, keep the budgets separate until the areas and scope are agreed. <a href="/vacancies/cmsfvflha000zoy01wxkk2efu">2 Kingfisher</a> remains flagged because its numeric area is 3,849 m&sup2; while its description states 3,300 m&sup2;; do not use it as a monthly-rent example until reconciled.</p>
<p>Next, use the <a href="/blog/compare-office-rental-quotes-midrand">office quote-comparison worksheet</a>, or <a href="/contact-us?interest=Office%20space#Contact">request an office quote and viewing</a> with your team brief, preferred date and budget.</p>$f0_4$, $f0_5$https://listings.blendproperty.co.za/uploads/listings/lst_import_954d405fa54ed9221351/e3c1a75d-f556-46b5-b45a-d1452aa44444-optimized.webp$f0_5$, $f0_6$Office Rental Costs in Midrand: Budget Guide$f0_6$, $f0_7$Build an office budget using published Midpoint examples. Separate base rent, services, parking, deposits and fit-out before requesting a full quote.$f0_7$, $f0_8$offices$f0_8$),
  ($f1_0$blog_office_quotes_20261019$f1_0$, $f1_1$compare-office-rental-quotes-midrand$f1_1$, $f1_2$How to Compare Office Rental Quotes in Midrand$f1_2$, $f1_3$Use the same area, charge, work and timing worksheet for each office quote, with unresolved figures kept visible.$f1_3$, $f1_4$<p>Compare office quotes using the same area basis, occupation date, lease period and workplace requirements. Two rates per square metre cannot tell you which office costs less to occupy if the quotes include different things.</p>
<p>Start with our <a href="/offices">Midrand office leasing guide</a> and use this worksheet when you have a shortlist. For an initial budget, read the <a href="/blog/office-rental-costs-midrand">office rental cost guide</a>.</p>
<h2>Give each quote a clear identity</h2>
<p>Record the building and unit, quote date, expiry or validity conditions, contact, advertised area and the proposed occupation date. Attach the plan or area schedule used for pricing. Confirm whether that area includes any shared or ancillary space rather than assuming every square metre is desk space.</p>
<p>For a dated source example, <a href="/vacancies/cmsfuu4xu000ooy01x3ulli7b">Unit 2, 2 Weaver Avenue</a> published 1,614.7 m&sup2; at R120 per m&sup2; per month when checked on 19 October 2026. That gives R193,764 in indicative monthly base rent. The calculation does not settle VAT, recoveries, services, fit-out or handover.</p>
<h2>Complete the same six lines for every option</h2>
<ol>
<li><strong>Area and base rent:</strong> record the agreed rentable area, measurement basis, rate per m&sup2; per month and resulting monthly amount. Flag any mismatch between the plan, schedule and quote.</li>
<li><strong>Recurring charges:</strong> list recoveries, utilities, parking, connectivity and other services. Mark whether each is included, separately priced, metered or awaiting confirmation.</li>
<li><strong>Initial payments:</strong> record the proposed deposit/security, advance payments and connection or setup charges, using the written offer rather than an assumed standard.</li>
<li><strong>Work and equipment:</strong> identify landlord and tenant work, furniture, cabling, equipment and relocation costs. Record any proposed contribution with its conditions.</li>
<li><strong>Timing:</strong> show the occupation date, required work, approvals, access for fit-out and when each quoted charge begins.</li>
<li><strong>Changes over the term:</strong> record agreed escalation dates, service limits, maintenance responsibilities and any reinstatement scope in the proposed terms.</li>
</ol>
<h2>Use consistent arithmetic</h2>
<p>Keep recurring monthly costs, once-off spending and refundable security in separate columns. Adding a deposit to monthly rent obscures the cash timing; excluding fit-out spending can obscure the upfront requirement. Where a charge is unknown, leave it visibly unresolved and request clarification.</p>
<p>For a period comparison, use the proposed monthly amounts for each month, reflecting any agreed changes at the correct dates. Do not multiply the opening rent by the whole term if the written proposal changes that figure later. Compare VAT on the same stated basis and have the treatment confirmed.</p>
<h2>Test whether both quotes solve the same problem</h2>
<p>A quote for a space with fitted meeting rooms may require a different scope from a largely open floor plate. The cheaper opening rent may come with work your team has not budgeted for. Use the <a href="/blog/office-viewing-checklist-midrand">viewing checklist</a> and <a href="/blog/office-floor-plan-fit-out-checklist-midrand">floor-plan checklist</a> to identify those differences.</p>
<p>If one option is serviced, use a <a href="/blog/onpoint-serviced-office-package-checklist">package inclusion checklist</a> as well. A serviced label does not establish what furniture, meeting use, connectivity or parking is included in the figure you were given.</p>
<h2>Resolve inconsistent figures before choosing</h2>
<p>Request a revised written quote where the area, rate, monthly amount or works scope conflicts. Arithmetic can reveal a mismatch but cannot establish which underlying figure is correct. For example, the warehouse/conversion listing at <a href="/vacancies/cmsfvflha000zoy01wxkk2efu">2 Kingfisher</a> remains flagged at 3,849 versus 3,300 m&sup2;; it is excluded from numeric rent examples until approved area and quote details agree.</p>
<p>Check the <a href="/vacancies?sector=Office">live office vacancies</a>, then <a href="/contact-us?interest=Office%20space#Contact">ask leasing for comparable written office quotes</a>. Include your preferred units, occupation date, layout needs and parking requirement.</p>$f1_4$, $f1_5$https://listings.blendproperty.co.za/uploads/listings/lst_import_8ea2c6eba0f41cc7f00f/7c3b5d13-e79f-431e-8924-94baa9da5fe7-optimized.webp$f1_5$, $f1_6$Compare Office Rental Quotes in Midrand$f1_6$, $f1_7$Compare office quotes on the same area, term, services and fit-out basis. Use a practical worksheet and current Midpoint office listings.$f1_7$, $f1_8$offices$f1_8$),
