<p>This article supports our <a href="/services-offices">OnPoint serviced-office guide</a> and links to the <a href="/offices">conventional office guide</a>. Midpoint publishes both leasing formats in Halfway House, Midrand; confirm the selected unit and package before committing.</p>
<h2>Start with how your team works</h2>
<p>Write down who will attend, when they will be present and which activities need private rooms. Include calls, visitors, confidential meetings, storage, equipment and accessibility needs. Then decide which facilities must be exclusive to your team and which can be shared under agreed booking rules.</p>
<p>This brief is more useful than choosing a label first. A team with frequent private meetings needs to understand room availability and charges. A business with a specific layout needs to understand fit-out permissions and responsibilities in either format.</p>
<h2>What the OnPoint listings actually advertise</h2>
<p>On 19 October 2026, the <a href="/vacancies/cms4oiw4n0002n601y2gpa0qf">OnPoint Office G.02 listing</a> published an area of 172.66 m&sup2; and asking rate of R117.50 per m&sup2; per month. Its features include furniture options, three meeting rooms, private call booths, shared kitchens, reception, monthly tenant credits and four covered parking bays.</p>
<p>Those are advertised listing features. They do not confirm that all facilities are exclusive, that a particular furniture choice is included, that meeting use is unlimited, or that credits cover a given service. Ask for the package schedule, allocation, booking conditions and separate charges. The <a href="/blog/onpoint-serviced-office-package-checklist">OnPoint package checklist</a> sets out what to request.</p>
<h2>What to check in a conventional office</h2>
<p>Start with the current floor plan, existing fit-out and required work. For example, the <a href="/vacancies/cms4oiw4v0004n60127izdqzj">Sunbird ground-floor listing</a> publishes 500.66 m&sup2; at R120 per m&sup2; per month and describes ground-floor accommodation. It does not establish a complete furniture, connectivity, parking or backup package.</p>
<p>Ask who supplies and maintains the services your operation depends on. Request a written scope for fit-out, cabling, furniture and any changes before occupation. Confirm the proposed term, deposit/security, charge start dates and occupation programme instead of assuming conventional terms are fixed or serviced terms are flexible.</p>
<h2>Compare the same workplace and cost basis</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Workspace:</strong> can the actual layout support your attendance, meetings, equipment and privacy needs?</li>
<li><strong>Services:</strong> which items are included, capped, bookable, metered or separately charged?</li>
<li><strong>Control and responsibility:</strong> who approves changes, handles maintenance and manages access or service issues?</li>
<li><strong>Timing:</strong> what is ready now, what work remains and when can the team occupy?</li>
<li><strong>Cost:</strong> compare the full quote and initial cash requirement, using the <a href="/blog/compare-office-rental-quotes-midrand">office quote worksheet</a>.</li>
</ul>
<p>These two published examples differ in area and configuration, so their asking rates do not prove that either format is cheaper. No verified like-for-like total package comparison is established here.</p>
<h2>View the options with one brief</h2>
<p>Use the <a href="/vacancies?sector=Serviced%20office">current serviced-office vacancies</a> and <a href="/vacancies?sector=Office">conventional office vacancies</a>, then confirm availability with leasing. Published photographs may show proposed works; inspect the actual space and agreed handover condition.</p>
<p><a href="/contact-us?interest=Serviced%20offices#Contact">Discuss a serviced-office requirement</a>, or <a href="/contact-us?interest=Office%20space#Contact">request conventional office options</a>. Bring the same team brief to both conversations.</p>$f2_4$, $f2_5$https://listings.blendproperty.co.za/uploads/listings/lst_onpoint_94411/f5154689-8c6e-4c72-b598-62f35fdf5400.webp$f2_5$, $f2_6$Serviced vs Conventional Offices in Midrand$f2_6$, $f2_7$Compare serviced and conventional offices by layout, services, responsibilities and full cost. Explore current Midpoint and OnPoint listings.$f2_7$, $f2_8$services-offices$f2_8$),
  ($f3_0$blog_serviced_package_20261019$f3_0$, $f3_1$onpoint-serviced-office-package-checklist$f3_1$, $f3_2$OnPoint Serviced Offices: Your Package Checklist$f3_2$, $f3_3$Turn advertised OnPoint features into a written package schedule covering allowances, booking rules, services, charges and occupation timing.$f3_3$, $f3_4$<p>Before choosing a serviced office, turn the advertised feature list into a written package schedule. For each service, confirm the allocation, limits, operating arrangements and cost for your team. The word “serviced” does not answer those questions on its own.</p>
<p>Use this checklist with the <a href="/services-offices">OnPoint serviced-office guide</a> and the specific <a href="/vacancies?sector=Serviced%20office">live serviced-office listings</a>. For a broader format comparison, read <a href="/blog/serviced-vs-conventional-offices-midrand">serviced versus conventional offices</a>.</p>
<h2>Confirm which suite and area are being quoted</h2>
<p>The <a href="/vacancies/cms4oiw530006n601h1qw8gzm">OnPoint Office G.07 listing</a>, checked on 19 October 2026, publishes 124.49 m&sup2; at R117.50 per m&sup2; per month and “Immediately” availability. These are listing statements, not a final package quote or confirmed handover date.</p>
<p>Ask for the current plan, agreed rentable area and exact suite identity. Check the furniture layout against attendance, storage, accessibility and privacy needs. An area figure does not establish how many people can safely or practically work there.</p>
<h2>Ask six package questions</h2>
<ol>
<li><strong>Furniture:</strong> the source advertises furnished or unfurnished options. Which items are supplied with this quote, in what condition and at what charge? Who handles changes or replacement?</li>
<li><strong>Meeting rooms and call booths:</strong> the source advertises three meeting rooms and private call booths. Confirm shared versus exclusive use, booking rules, included allowances, opening hours and any extra-use charges.</li>
<li><strong>Tenant credits:</strong> monthly tenant credits appear in the listing. Request the value, eligible services, expiry or carry-over rules and the charge once credits are used. No specific allowance is established by the feature label.</li>
<li><strong>Parking and access:</strong> the source lists four covered parking bays. Confirm the allocation to this suite, whether charges are included, visitor arrangements, access hours and any additional-bay options.</li>
<li><strong>Connectivity and backup:</strong> request the actual connectivity provision, support arrangements and any separate charges. Confirm which equipment and circuits have backup, capacity and operating limits; shared estate features do not establish this unit’s coverage.</li>
<li><strong>Shared facilities:</strong> the source lists kitchens, reception and an on-site barista. Confirm the current service, operating hours, allocation, permitted use and any charges rather than assuming unlimited inclusion.</li>
</ol>
<h2>Compare cost and responsibility together</h2>
<p>Ask for base rent, VAT treatment, recoveries, utilities and every applicable service charge on the same schedule. Mark each line as included, separately priced, capped, metered, not applicable or awaiting confirmation. Keep deposit/security and setup spending separate from the recurring monthly total.</p>
<p>Record who deals with connectivity, furniture, access and maintenance issues. A service without an agreed scope or responsible contact can leave an operational question unresolved even if it appears in promotional copy.</p>
<h2>Confirm readiness and the written terms</h2>
<p>Agree the proposed term, occupation date, any required work, charge start dates and the process for changing your space or service use. Do not assume a serviced-office arrangement can be cancelled at any time or expanded on demand. Have the written terms reviewed by your own advisers where needed.</p>
<p>Use the <a href="/blog/office-viewing-checklist-midrand">office viewing checklist</a> to inspect the suite, and the <a href="/blog/compare-office-rental-quotes-midrand">quote-comparison worksheet</a> to compare it with another option. Package features and availability can change after this article’s source check.</p>
