<p>Use this checklist alongside our <a href="/offices">offices to rent in Midrand guide</a> and <a href="/vacancies?sector=Office">current office vacancies</a>. If you need a serviced suite, also check the <a href="/services-offices">OnPoint guide</a> and its package conditions.</p>
<h2>Before the visit: send a short brief</h2>
<p>Tell leasing your expected attendance, private-office and meeting-room needs, visitor volumes, parking requirement, critical equipment, target move date and budget. Include access or accessibility needs and any work that must happen before occupation.</p>
<p>Ask for the exact unit reference, current floor plan, published area, asking rate, availability and a list of existing versus proposed work. Confirm which entrance to use through the <a href="/location">estate location page</a> and your viewing contact. Do not treat gate access as evidence of staffed leasing or tenant operating hours.</p>
<h2>Walk the daily route</h2>
<ol>
<li><strong>Arrival:</strong> check the intended entrance, parking allocation, visitor process and route to the office with the people who will use it.</li>
<li><strong>Working area:</strong> compare the actual layout with your attendance, storage, private calls and meeting needs. Note fixed features and obstructions that affect the plan.</li>
<li><strong>Building services:</strong> ask about connectivity, electrical provision, ventilation or cooling, water and support arrangements for this unit. Arrange appropriate technical checks for critical requirements.</li>
<li><strong>Backup:</strong> confirm the supported equipment/circuits, allocation and operating arrangements. A generator or backup-water label does not establish uninterrupted service to every tenant use.</li>
<li><strong>Fit-out and condition:</strong> record what exists, what is proposed, who will do the work and what must be agreed before handover.</li>
<li><strong>Costs and dates:</strong> request the complete quote, area basis, term and occupation programme. Record unresolved points rather than treating a verbal estimate as final.</li>
</ol>
<h2>Use the listing as a starting record</h2>
<p>For example, <a href="/vacancies/cms4oiw4v0004n60127izdqzj">Sunbird ground-floor office</a> published 500.66 m&sup2;, an asking rate of R120 per m&sup2; per month and immediate availability when checked on 19 October 2026. Its description identifies ground-floor accommodation and a minimum lease of 12 months. Confirm that the current offer and handover match those statements.</p>
<p><a href="/vacancies/cms4oiw500005n6011rnzc2hb">Unit 1, 1 Weaver Avenue</a> is another published office option. Request its current plan and visit the specific suite rather than assuming its layout or service allocation matches Sunbird. Listing photographs may include proposed works and do not replace a condition check.</p>
<h2>Leave with documents and named actions</h2>
<p>Request the current dimensioned plan, confirmed rentable-area schedule, fit-out scope, specification/service schedule and complete written quote. Record who will resolve each outstanding item and by when. The <a href="/blog/office-floor-plan-fit-out-checklist-midrand">floor-plan checklist</a> helps assess the layout; the <a href="/blog/compare-office-rental-quotes-midrand">quote worksheet</a> helps compare costs.</p>
<p>If you also inspect warehouse or conversion space, do not let that enquiry inherit office assumptions. The <a href="/vacancies/cmsfvflha000zoy01wxkk2efu">2 Kingfisher area conflict</a> remains unresolved at 3,849 versus 3,300 m&sup2;; obtain the approved schedule and plans before using an area or monthly-rent calculation.</p>
